            'Surface pressure is determined solely by the molecular weight of the dominant atmospheric gas: N₂ (molecular weight 28) is heavier than Earth\'s predominantly O₂ + N₂ mixture (effective molecular weight ~29), so Titan\'s pressure is approximately equal to Earth\'s; the 50% difference is within the uncertainties of pre-Cassini models and is not actually explained by gravity differences; the Huygens probe confirmed that surface pressure is 1.467 bar, slightly below Earth\'s, correcting earlier overestimates',
